---
title: Migrating
description: Move an existing visualization to TanStack Charts by preserving analytical semantics, interaction behavior, and measurable output before changing design.
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migration is a semantic exercise, not a component-name translation. First\ndescribe what the existing chart means and how users operate it. Then express\nthat behavior with data preparation, scales, marks, and host options."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"move-pre-alpha-root-scales-into-the-registry","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Move pre-Alpha root scales into the registry"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alpha definitions require Cartesian scale and axis options under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scales"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: xScale },\n    y: { scale: yScale, grid: true },\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When updating from a pre-Alpha release, move root "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scales.x"},{"type":"text","value":" and root\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scales.y"},{"type":"text","value":". Every definition must provide both reserved entries. Use\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" when the chart does not use one of the Cartesian dimensions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Polar definitions follow the same migration. Move pre-Alpha root "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"angle"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"radius"},{"type":"text","value":" options into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"polar({ scales: { angle, radius } })"},{"type":"text","value":". Every polar\ndefinition must provide both reserved entries. If neither positional scale is\nused, write "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scales: { angle: null, radius: null }"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom mark type code should replace "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkX"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkY"},{"type":"text","value":" with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkPointX"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkPointY"},{"type":"text","value":" from\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/mark/scale-values"},{"type":"text","value":". A polar length callback should replace\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"layout.angle"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"layout.scales.angle"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"layout.radiusScale"},{"type":"text","value":" with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"layout.scales.radius"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"inventory-the-current-contract","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inventory the current contract"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Record:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"input rows and derived fields;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"sorting, grouping, bins, stacks, and normalization;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"x, y, color, size, and grouping semantics;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"domain, baseline, padding, curve, and missing-value policy;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"axes, labels, legends, annotations, and margins;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tooltip grouping and formatting;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"pointer, keyboard, selection, zoom, and playback behavior;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"responsive breakpoints and first-render size;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"animation identity and interruption behavior;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"accessible name, summary, and table;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"current bundle and performance measurements."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Screenshots alone do not capture these decisions."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"preserve-transforms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preserve transforms"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep proven application, server, SQL, or D3 transforms for the first migration.\nPass their output to marks directly. Rewriting analytical logic at the same\ntime makes it difficult to tell whether a visual difference is a renderer\nregression or a changed calculation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Move or simplify transforms only after parity is measured. The dependency\nboundary is explained in "},{"type":"link","href":"../concepts/scales-and-d3.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scales"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"translate-to-the-grammar","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Translate to the grammar"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Map each visible layer independently:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"line or area series;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"bars, rectangles, or cells;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"dots or hexagons;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"rules, links, ticks, arrows, or vectors;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"text and frame annotations;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"facet panels."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Then assign explicit scales and guides. Complex charts are usually several\nordinary marks sharing a coordinate system, not one specialized chart type."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"consolidate-package-imports","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Consolidate package imports"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts"},{"type":"text","value":" once and keep the framework peers and D3 modules\nthat application source imports directly. Move TanStack scale and adapter\nimports to package subpaths:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Previous import"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current import"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts-scales/<family>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/scales/<family>"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-charts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/react"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-charts/<capability>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/react/<capability>"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-native-charts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/react-native"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-native-charts/tooltip"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/react-native/tooltip"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/octane-charts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/octane"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/octane-charts/<capability>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/octane/<capability>"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/<framework>-charts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/<framework>"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same mapping applies to React and Octane "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/core"},{"type":"text","value":" entries and React\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/tooltip"},{"type":"text","value":". Exact ESM entry graphs and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sideEffects: false"},{"type":"text","value":" preserve capability\nand framework tree shaking inside the single published package."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For the current breaking API:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"move axis presentation under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"axis"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"axis: false"},{"type":"text","value":" to hide one axis while retaining its scale;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"move candidate count and formatting under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"axis.ticks"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"move rotation and thinning under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"axis.tickLabels"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"use a single bar/area value as stack length, explicit endpoints to opt out,\nand "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"layout: group()"},{"type":"text","value":" for side-by-side bars;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"replace renderer-specific focus decoration with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"whenFocused"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"replace duration-only spring approximations with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion({ transition: { type: 'spring', ... } })"},{"type":"text","value":" and put chart-, mark-,\ndatum-, or guide-specific policy on the definition;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"type: 'tween'"},{"type":"text","value":" to focus-state transitions that previously supplied only\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"duration"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"easing"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"replace channel "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(datum, index, data)"},{"type":"text","value":" accessors with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(datum, { index, data })"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"replace facet "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chart(data, key)"},{"type":"text","value":" builders with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chart(data, { key })"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"replace focus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolve(points, x, y, maxDistance)"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group(points, point)"},{"type":"text","value":" implementations with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolve(points, context)"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group(points, { point })"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"replace spatial-index "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(points, scene)"},{"type":"text","value":" factories with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(points, { scene })"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"replace legend "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height(itemCount, width, colors)"},{"type":"text","value":" implementations with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height(itemCount, context)"},{"type":"text","value":". The previous "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" value is now\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context.chart.width"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"replace controlled-signal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(value, reason)"},{"type":"text","value":" callbacks with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(value, { reason })"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"replace keyed-selection "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key(datum, point)"},{"type":"text","value":" callbacks with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key(datum, { point })"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"replace focus-guide "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"format(value, point)"},{"type":"text","value":" callbacks with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"format(value, { point })"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"replace interactive-legend "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"itemAriaLabel(value, visible)"},{"type":"text","value":" callbacks with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"itemAriaLabel(value, { visible })"},{"type":"text","value":"; and"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"use the second "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTooltipContentContext"},{"type":"text","value":" argument in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"format"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formatGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" when formatter output depends on pinned state or axis\nformatting."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"../concepts/marks-and-layering.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Marks and Layering"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../examples/index.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example Gallery"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"establish-parity-gates","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Establish parity gates"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the same frozen data and dimensions on both implementations. Compare:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"prepared values and scale domains;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"representative geometry and baselines;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"bar bandwidth and alignment;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"line gaps and curve crossings;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"axis ticks, rotation, titles, and automatic margins;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tooltip rows, colors, and formatted values;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"focus, selection, and keyboard paths;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"light and dark output;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"update, resize, and reorder state preservation;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"production bundle and render/update measurements."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefer numeric and behavioral assertions. Use screenshot diffs for the\nremaining painted details."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"migrate-incrementally","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migrate incrementally"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A reliable order is:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render a static, fixed-size chart."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Match scales, marks, and guides."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add responsive sizing and automatic margins."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Match tooltip and keyboard focus."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Match selection and controlled viewport state."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Capture live values in framework-memoized definitions."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add animation."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Measure production bundles and update performance."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Remove the old renderer after the parity suite passes."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep a temporary renderer switch only as a migration verification tool with a\ndefined removal gate. It should not become permanent application architecture."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"know-what-not-to-migrate","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Know what not to migrate"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not preserve accidental internals:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"generated DOM structure;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"private renderer hooks;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"broad package imports;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"pixel constants compensating for clipped labels;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"unstable array-index keys;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"manual tooltips that duplicate the default focus model."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preserve user-visible meaning and behavior. Replace implementation accidents\nwith the documented TanStack Charts boundary."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"close-the-migration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Close the migration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before deleting the old path:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"all chart modes and empty states have parity coverage;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"accessibility and reduced motion pass;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"representative production data has been exercised;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the new path meets explicit bundle and performance budgets;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"rollback is a version or commit, not two live renderers;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"newly discovered API friction is resolved or documented at the correct\nlayer."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"./testing-and-debugging.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Testing and Debugging"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./bundle-size-and-performance.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bundle Size and Performance"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"move-pre-alpha-root-scales-into-the-registry","text":"Move pre-Alpha root scales into the registry","level":2},{"id":"inventory-the-current-contract","text":"Inventory the current contract","level":2},{"id":"preserve-transforms","text":"Preserve transforms","level":2},{"id":"translate-to-the-grammar","text":"Translate to the grammar","level":2},{"id":"consolidate-package-imports","text":"Consolidate package imports","level":2},{"id":"establish-parity-gates","text":"Establish parity gates","level":2},{"id":"migrate-incrementally","text":"Migrate incrementally","level":2},{"id":"know-what-not-to-migrate","text":"Know what not to migrate","level":2},{"id":"close-the-migration","text":"Close the migration","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nMigration is a semantic exercise, not a component-name translation. First\ndescribe what the existing chart means and how users operate it. Then express\nthat behavior with data preparation, scales, marks, and host options.\n\n## Move pre-Alpha root scales into the registry\n\nAlpha definitions require Cartesian scale and axis options under `scales`:\n\n```ts\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: xScale },\n    y: { scale: yScale, grid: true },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nWhen updating from a pre-Alpha release, move root `x` to `scales.x` and root\n`y` to `scales.y`. Every definition must provide both reserved entries. Use\n`null` when the chart does not use one of the Cartesian dimensions.\n\nPolar definitions follow the same migration. Move pre-Alpha root `angle` and\n`radius` options into `polar({ scales: { angle, radius } })`. Every polar\ndefinition must provide both reserved entries. If neither positional scale is\nused, write `scales: { angle: null, radius: null }`.\n\nCustom mark type code should replace `ChartMarkX` and `ChartMarkY` with\n`ChartMarkPointX` and `ChartMarkPointY` from\n`@tanstack/charts/mark/scale-values`. A polar length callback should replace\n`layout.angle` with `layout.scales.angle` and `layout.radiusScale` with\n`layout.scales.radius`.\n\n## Inventory the current contract\n\nRecord:\n\n- input rows and derived fields;\n- sorting, grouping, bins, stacks, and normalization;\n- x, y, color, size, and grouping semantics;\n- domain, baseline, padding, curve, and missing-value policy;\n- axes, labels, legends, annotations, and margins;\n- tooltip grouping and formatting;\n- pointer, keyboard, selection, zoom, and playback behavior;\n- responsive breakpoints and first-render size;\n- animation identity and interruption behavior;\n- accessible name, summary, and table;\n- current bundle and performance measurements.\n\nScreenshots alone do not capture these decisions.\n\n## Preserve transforms\n\nKeep proven application, server, SQL, or D3 transforms for the first migration.\nPass their output to marks directly. Rewriting analytical logic at the same\ntime makes it difficult to tell whether a visual difference is a renderer\nregression or a changed calculation.\n\nMove or simplify transforms only after parity is measured. The dependency\nboundary is explained in [Scales](../concepts/scales-and-d3.md).\n\n## Translate to the grammar\n\nMap each visible layer independently:\n\n- line or area series;\n- bars, rectangles, or cells;\n- dots or hexagons;\n- rules, links, ticks, arrows, or vectors;\n- text and frame annotations;\n- facet panels.\n\nThen assign explicit scales and guides. Complex charts are usually several\nordinary marks sharing a coordinate system, not one specialized chart type.\n\n## Consolidate package imports\n\nInstall `@tanstack/charts` once and keep the framework peers and D3 modules\nthat application source imports directly. Move TanStack scale and adapter\nimports to package subpaths:\n\n| Previous import                         | Current import                          |\n| --------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `@tanstack/charts-scales/<family>`      | `@tanstack/charts/scales/<family>`      |\n| `@tanstack/react-charts`                | `@tanstack/charts/react`                |\n| `@tanstack/react-charts/<capability>`   | `@tanstack/charts/react/<capability>`   |\n| `@tanstack/react-native-charts`         | `@tanstack/charts/react-native`         |\n| `@tanstack/react-native-charts/tooltip` | `@tanstack/charts/react-native/tooltip` |\n| `@tanstack/octane-charts`               | `@tanstack/charts/octane`               |\n| `@tanstack/octane-charts/<capability>`  | `@tanstack/charts/octane/<capability>`  |\n| `@tanstack/<framework>-charts`          | `@tanstack/charts/<framework>`          |\n\nThe same mapping applies to React and Octane `/core` entries and React\n`/tooltip`. Exact ESM entry graphs and `sideEffects: false` preserve capability\nand framework tree shaking inside the single published package.\n\nFor the current breaking API:\n\n- move axis presentation under `axis`;\n- use `axis: false` to hide one axis while retaining its scale;\n- move candidate count and formatting under `axis.ticks`;\n- move rotation and thinning under `axis.tickLabels`;\n- use a single bar/area value as stack length, explicit endpoints to opt out,\n  and `layout: group()` for side-by-side bars;\n- replace renderer-specific focus decoration with `whenFocused`.\n- replace duration-only spring approximations with\n  `motion({ transition: { type: 'spring', ... } })` and put chart-, mark-,\n  datum-, or guide-specific policy on the definition;\n- add `type: 'tween'` to focus-state transitions that previously supplied only\n  `duration` and `easing`.\n- replace channel `(datum, index, data)` accessors with\n  `(datum, { index, data })`;\n- replace facet `chart(data, key)` builders with `chart(data, { key })`;\n- replace focus `resolve(points, x, y, maxDistance)` and\n  `group(points, point)` implementations with `resolve(points, context)` and\n  `group(points, { point })`;\n- replace spatial-index `(points, scene)` factories with\n  `(points, { scene })`;\n- replace legend `height(itemCount, width, colors)` implementations with\n  `height(itemCount, context)`. The previous `width` value is now\n  `context.chart.width`;\n- replace controlled-signal `(value, reason)` callbacks with\n  `(value, { reason })`;\n- replace keyed-selection `key(datum, point)` callbacks with\n  `key(datum, { point })`;\n- replace focus-guide `format(value, point)` callbacks with\n  `format(value, { point })`;\n- replace interactive-legend `itemAriaLabel(value, visible)` callbacks with\n  `itemAriaLabel(value, { visible })`; and\n- use the second `ChartTooltipContentContext` argument in `format` and\n  `formatGroup` when formatter output depends on pinned state or axis\n  formatting.\n\nSee [Marks and Layering](../concepts/marks-and-layering.md) and the\n[Example Gallery](../examples/index.md).\n\n## Establish parity gates\n\nUse the same frozen data and dimensions on both implementations. Compare:\n\n- prepared values and scale domains;\n- representative geometry and baselines;\n- bar bandwidth and alignment;\n- line gaps and curve crossings;\n- axis ticks, rotation, titles, and automatic margins;\n- tooltip rows, colors, and formatted values;\n- focus, selection, and keyboard paths;\n- light and dark output;\n- update, resize, and reorder state preservation;\n- production bundle and render/update measurements.\n\nPrefer numeric and behavioral assertions. Use screenshot diffs for the\nremaining painted details.\n\n## Migrate incrementally\n\nA reliable order is:\n\n1. Render a static, fixed-size chart.\n2. Match scales, marks, and guides.\n3. Add responsive sizing and automatic margins.\n4. Match tooltip and keyboard focus.\n5. Match selection and controlled viewport state.\n6. Capture live values in framework-memoized definitions.\n7. Add animation.\n8. Measure production bundles and update performance.\n9. Remove the old renderer after the parity suite passes.\n\nKeep a temporary renderer switch only as a migration verification tool with a\ndefined removal gate. It should not become permanent application architecture.\n\n## Know what not to migrate\n\nDo not preserve accidental internals:\n\n- generated DOM structure;\n- private renderer hooks;\n- broad package imports;\n- pixel constants compensating for clipped labels;\n- unstable array-index keys;\n- manual tooltips that duplicate the default focus model.\n\nPreserve user-visible meaning and behavior. Replace implementation accidents\nwith the documented TanStack Charts boundary.\n\n## Close the migration\n\nBefore deleting the old path:\n\n- all chart modes and empty states have parity coverage;\n- accessibility and reduced motion pass;\n- representative production data has been exercised;\n- the new path meets explicit bundle and performance budgets;\n- rollback is a version or commit, not two live renderers;\n- newly discovered API friction is resolved or documented at the correct\n  layer.\n\nSee [Testing and Debugging](./testing-and-debugging.md) and\n[Bundle Size and Performance](./bundle-size-and-performance.md).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Migrating\ndescription: Move an existing visualization to TanStack Charts by preserving analytical semantics, interaction behavior, and measurable output before changing design.\n---\n\nMigration is a semantic exercise, not a component-name translation. First\ndescribe what the existing chart means and how users operate it. Then express\nthat behavior with data preparation, scales, marks, and host options.\n\n## Move pre-Alpha root scales into the registry\n\nAlpha definitions require Cartesian scale and axis options under `scales`:\n\n```ts\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: xScale },\n    y: { scale: yScale, grid: true },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nWhen updating from a pre-Alpha release, move root `x` to `scales.x` and root\n`y` to `scales.y`. Every definition must provide both reserved entries. Use\n`null` when the chart does not use one of the Cartesian dimensions.\n\nPolar definitions follow the same migration. Move pre-Alpha root `angle` and\n`radius` options into `polar({ scales: { angle, radius } })`. Every polar\ndefinition must provide both reserved entries. If neither positional scale is\nused, write `scales: { angle: null, radius: null }`.\n\nCustom mark type code should replace `ChartMarkX` and `ChartMarkY` with\n`ChartMarkPointX` and `ChartMarkPointY` from\n`@tanstack/charts/mark/scale-values`. A polar length callback should replace\n`layout.angle` with `layout.scales.angle` and `layout.radiusScale` with\n`layout.scales.radius`.\n\n## Inventory the current contract\n\nRecord:\n\n- input rows and derived fields;\n- sorting, grouping, bins, stacks, and normalization;\n- x, y, color, size, and grouping semantics;\n- domain, baseline, padding, curve, and missing-value policy;\n- axes, labels, legends, annotations, and margins;\n- tooltip grouping and formatting;\n- pointer, keyboard, selection, zoom, and playback behavior;\n- responsive breakpoints and first-render size;\n- animation identity and interruption behavior;\n- accessible name, summary, and table;\n- current bundle and performance measurements.\n\nScreenshots alone do not capture these decisions.\n\n## Preserve transforms\n\nKeep proven application, server, SQL, or D3 transforms for the first migration.\nPass their output to marks directly. Rewriting analytical logic at the same\ntime makes it difficult to tell whether a visual difference is a renderer\nregression or a changed calculation.\n\nMove or simplify transforms only after parity is measured. The dependency\nboundary is explained in [Scales](../concepts/scales-and-d3.md).\n\n## Translate to the grammar\n\nMap each visible layer independently:\n\n- line or area series;\n- bars, rectangles, or cells;\n- dots or hexagons;\n- rules, links, ticks, arrows, or vectors;\n- text and frame annotations;\n- facet panels.\n\nThen assign explicit scales and guides. Complex charts are usually several\nordinary marks sharing a coordinate system, not one specialized chart type.\n\n## Consolidate package imports\n\nInstall `@tanstack/charts` once and keep the framework peers and D3 modules\nthat application source imports directly. Move TanStack scale and adapter\nimports to package subpaths:\n\n| Previous import                         | Current import                          |\n| --------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `@tanstack/charts-scales/<family>`      | `@tanstack/charts/scales/<family>`      |\n| `@tanstack/react-charts`                | `@tanstack/charts/react`                |\n| `@tanstack/react-charts/<capability>`   | `@tanstack/charts/react/<capability>`   |\n| `@tanstack/react-native-charts`         | `@tanstack/charts/react-native`         |\n| `@tanstack/react-native-charts/tooltip` | `@tanstack/charts/react-native/tooltip` |\n| `@tanstack/octane-charts`               | `@tanstack/charts/octane`               |\n| `@tanstack/octane-charts/<capability>`  | `@tanstack/charts/octane/<capability>`  |\n| `@tanstack/<framework>-charts`          | `@tanstack/charts/<framework>`          |\n\nThe same mapping applies to React and Octane `/core` entries and React\n`/tooltip`. Exact ESM entry graphs and `sideEffects: false` preserve capability\nand framework tree shaking inside the single published package.\n\nFor the current breaking API:\n\n- move axis presentation under `axis`;\n- use `axis: false` to hide one axis while retaining its scale;\n- move candidate count and formatting under `axis.ticks`;\n- move rotation and thinning under `axis.tickLabels`;\n- use a single bar/area value as stack length, explicit endpoints to opt out,\n  and `layout: group()` for side-by-side bars;\n- replace renderer-specific focus decoration with `whenFocused`.\n- replace duration-only spring approximations with\n  `motion({ transition: { type: 'spring', ... } })` and put chart-, mark-,\n  datum-, or guide-specific policy on the definition;\n- add `type: 'tween'` to focus-state transitions that previously supplied only\n  `duration` and `easing`.\n- replace channel `(datum, index, data)` accessors with\n  `(datum, { index, data })`;\n- replace facet `chart(data, key)` builders with `chart(data, { key })`;\n- replace focus `resolve(points, x, y, maxDistance)` and\n  `group(points, point)` implementations with `resolve(points, context)` and\n  `group(points, { point })`;\n- replace spatial-index `(points, scene)` factories with\n  `(points, { scene })`;\n- replace legend `height(itemCount, width, colors)` implementations with\n  `height(itemCount, context)`. The previous `width` value is now\n  `context.chart.width`;\n- replace controlled-signal `(value, reason)` callbacks with\n  `(value, { reason })`;\n- replace keyed-selection `key(datum, point)` callbacks with\n  `key(datum, { point })`;\n- replace focus-guide `format(value, point)` callbacks with\n  `format(value, { point })`;\n- replace interactive-legend `itemAriaLabel(value, visible)` callbacks with\n  `itemAriaLabel(value, { visible })`; and\n- use the second `ChartTooltipContentContext` argument in `format` and\n  `formatGroup` when formatter output depends on pinned state or axis\n  formatting.\n\nSee [Marks and Layering](../concepts/marks-and-layering.md) and the\n[Example Gallery](../examples/index.md).\n\n## Establish parity gates\n\nUse the same frozen data and dimensions on both implementations. Compare:\n\n- prepared values and scale domains;\n- representative geometry and baselines;\n- bar bandwidth and alignment;\n- line gaps and curve crossings;\n- axis ticks, rotation, titles, and automatic margins;\n- tooltip rows, colors, and formatted values;\n- focus, selection, and keyboard paths;\n- light and dark output;\n- update, resize, and reorder state preservation;\n- production bundle and render/update measurements.\n\nPrefer numeric and behavioral assertions. Use screenshot diffs for the\nremaining painted details.\n\n## Migrate incrementally\n\nA reliable order is:\n\n1. Render a static, fixed-size chart.\n2. Match scales, marks, and guides.\n3. Add responsive sizing and automatic margins.\n4. Match tooltip and keyboard focus.\n5. Match selection and controlled viewport state.\n6. Capture live values in framework-memoized definitions.\n7. Add animation.\n8. Measure production bundles and update performance.\n9. Remove the old renderer after the parity suite passes.\n\nKeep a temporary renderer switch only as a migration verification tool with a\ndefined removal gate. It should not become permanent application architecture.\n\n## Know what not to migrate\n\nDo not preserve accidental internals:\n\n- generated DOM structure;\n- private renderer hooks;\n- broad package imports;\n- pixel constants compensating for clipped labels;\n- unstable array-index keys;\n- manual tooltips that duplicate the default focus model.\n\nPreserve user-visible meaning and behavior. Replace implementation accidents\nwith the documented TanStack Charts boundary.\n\n## Close the migration\n\nBefore deleting the old path:\n\n- all chart modes and empty states have parity coverage;\n- accessibility and reduced motion pass;\n- representative production data has been exercised;\n- the new path meets explicit bundle and performance budgets;\n- rollback is a version or commit, not two live renderers;\n- newly discovered API friction is resolved or documented at the correct\n  layer.\n\nSee [Testing and Debugging](./testing-and-debugging.md) and\n[Bundle Size and Performance](./bundle-size-and-performance.md).\n"}
